        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most homes need one cord: a 25-foot, 10-gauge L14-30 cord such as the Champion Power Equipment 25-Foot model, running from the generator to an inlet box and transfer switch. Large generators with a 14-50 outlet need the CircleCord 50-amp cord, inverters with an RV outlet need a TT-30 cord, and homes without a transfer switch do best with the Champion splitter cord and a few 12-gauge appliance cords.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, match the plug to the generator, the far end to the inlet, the gauge to the amps and the length to a safe generator spot at least 20 feet from the house. Then store the cord with the generator, so it is there when the lights go out.
          </p>
